**/js/dist/**/* -diff
**/js/dist/**/* linguist-generated
**/js/dist-typings/**/* -diff
**/js/dist-typings/**/* linguist-generated
**/js/yarn.lock -diff
**/js/package-lock.json -diff

* text=auto eol=lf

# After the catch-all above, because the last matching line wins: the IP dataset is read byte
# by byte at fixed offsets, so `text=auto` must never get the chance to guess at it. `binary`
# is `-text -diff`, which rules out both line-ending translation and a diff nobody could read
# anyway. Git's own heuristic would reach the same conclusion from the NUL bytes, but a record
# boundary is not a thing to leave to a guess.
**/resources/*.dat binary
**/resources/*.dat linguist-generated
**/tests/fixtures/**/*.dat binary
